# New Reno and headquarters (Umsetzung 7)
{150}{}{The widow Varga found out the deed is forged. She's waiting at the Garter, and she wants to talk about money.}
{151}{}{The widow told all of Virgin Street that the Garter stands on a forged deed. The families are laughing. Some of them are taking notes.}
{152}{}{The families are sitting down at the Garter. Asch is keeping a chair free for you.}
{153}{}{Nobody sat at the table for us. The families decided without us.}
{154}{}{Westin's people took Bishop's letter without a word. Pagano will want to know.}
{155}{}{The Mordinos' contract is worthless now. There's nobody left who could sign for them.}

# Redding (Umsetzung 8)
{160}{}{Sheriff Marion found the rigged scale. By midnight the miners had torn the counter out of the floor. The Slag stays shut for three weeks, and Ascorti wants double.}
{161}{}{The Malamute gave up the girls upstairs. Four weeks of our prices were more than they could stand.}
{162}{}{The Wanamingo mine is clean. Sheriff Marion let it be known that the Slag is under his protection now.}

# Vault City (Umsetzung 9)
{170}{}{The Garde came down the cellar stairs at dawn. }
{171}{}{A guard at the gate says the Garde is coming to the Courtyard next week. Hanne wants to talk.}
{172}{}{The Garde searched the boarding house and found clean sheets and a locked, empty cellar. They left without a word.}
{173}{}{Somebody found the File. The Garde came the same night.}
{174}{}{ of our people are in the Corrections Center now. After that comes the Servant Allocation Center.}

# NCR (Umsetzung 10)
{180}{}{The license came: "Licensed Establishment No. 9 of the Republic." Dora is painting the number over the door.}
{181}{}{A health inspector came, found no infirmary, and wrote the Trough up. Until there's an infirmary, the license is suspended.}
{182}{}{An infirmary and clean papers: The Trough is licensed again.}
{183}{}{Leaflets all over the Bazaar: CLOSE THE PENS, CLOSE THE HOUSES. The League for a Pure Republic has a picket line in front of the Trough.}
{184}{}{The Council will hear a decency law that would revoke every license in the Republic. Dora wants to talk.}
{185}{}{The Trough is burning. Somebody threw a firebomb through the back window.}
{186}{}{Nobody put out the fire in time. The upper floor is gone. It'll take a month before the Trough is what it was.}
{188}{}{The decency law passed with an exception everyone calls Lex Nine: registered houses with fair shares, examinations and no forced labor may stay open. The unlicensed ones close. Ruth Calloway checks the Trough's books every month.}
{189}{}{The League for a Pure Republic is finished. Nobody hands out leaflets in the Bazaar anymore, and nobody asks what happened to its people.}
{192}{}{The decency law passed without exceptions. The Trough has no license now. It keeps working, the way everything illegal in the Republic keeps working.}
{193}{}{The decency law failed in the Council. The League still hands out leaflets, but fewer people take them.}
{195}{}{The Rangers raided the Trough and freed everyone Vortis sold you. The license is gone, and the Rangers will not forget your name.}
{196}{}{The Council heard the decency law without us. Nobody spoke for the Trough.}

# San Francisco (Umsetzung 11)
{197}{}{Inspectors of the Shi came with lanterns and found the smugglers' room. The Seal is withdrawn, the tribute goes up, and the goods are gone.}
{198}{}{The tanker crew found out who the Bilge reports to. Nobody from the tanker drinks here anymore.}

# Blood on Virgin Street (Umsetzung 12)
{200}{}{Carlo Venuti from the Desperado is sitting at the bar. He says he's here about the neighborhood.}
{201}{}{A woman from the Cat's Paw is asking for you. Miss Kitty sent her.}
{202}{}{Venuti waited, and nobody came. He took the silence as an answer.}
{203}{}{Two of ours have pinpoint pupils and new friends. Somebody is selling Jet inside the Garter.}
{204}{}{Venuti is back at the Garter, and he brought men who don't sit down.}
{205}{}{Venuti's men came at night while nobody was there to stop them. The Garter is shut for two weeks.}
{206}{}{The Mordinos have fallen. Nobody on Virgin Street is collecting for the Desperado anymore.}
{207}{}{The families sat down without the Mordinos and divided Virgin Street again. The Garter's name was on the table. Nobody crossed it out.}
{208}{}{One of ours went over to Kitty's Claw. Kitty pays well, and she never forgets.}

# Talents (Umsetzung 13)
{210}{}{In Gecko an old ghoul closes the lid of a battered piano and packs a single suitcase. Vesper is on her way to the Silver Garter.}
{211}{}{Vesper sang tonight. Nobody in the room said a word until she stopped.}
{212}{}{Vesper stands in the hall and looks at the empty corner where the stage used to be. She'll sing when there is a stage again.}
{213}{}{Vesper is gone. She said she has heard enough people cry behind locked doors for one lifetime.}
{214}{}{Marcus opened the cell himself and shook the mutant's hand. Talus is on his way to you.}
{215}{}{The cell in Broken Hills is empty. Talus is on his way to you. Marcus knows who opened it, and the road through Broken Hills is closed to your runners.}
{216}{}{Talus is still in Marcus' cell. Marcus won't open it until somebody finds out what really happened to the missing people.}
{217}{}{A super mutant stands at the door now. Nobody has tried to start a fight since.}
{218}{}{Talus saw the bolt on the outside of the cellar door. He put down his club, walked to Broken Hills and told Marcus everything.}
{219}{}{Julian relapsed. The infirmary kept him alive. He won't look anyone in the eye.}
{220}{}{Julian died in the back room. Nobody came with a needle or a doctor. They found him in the morning.}
{221}{}{The new infirmary pulled Julian through. He came back. Some of him didn't.}
{222}{}{Abigail went to the Garde. She knew every name and every stair, and she told them all.}
{223}{}{Julian is gone. He left a note: "Thanks for the rooms. Not for the rest."}
{224}{}{Julian relapsed. He is lying in a back room, barely breathing. Without a doctor he won't last the week.}

# Jobs and the runners' road (Umsetzung 14)
{230}{}{Tyler is gone. Nobody collects for looking the other way anymore.}
{232}{}{Marcus is dead. Broken Hills closes its gates to anyone who works for you, and every town along the road hears why.}
{233}{}{Marcus has heard what you are. Your runners take the long way around Broken Hills now.}
